{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/848879-question-about-storytelling-the-invictus","id":848879,"title":"Question about storytelling the Invictus","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-03-17T10:59:01-07:00","id":848879,"title":"Question about storytelling the Invictus","content":"I'm curious how other ST's handle the Invictus in their campaigns, specifically if and how they play up the titles aspect, and if so, how? Do you guys just hand wave that covenant members know and are implied to be using everyone's titles, or do you actually expect players that chose to join to study and use them co\u0155rectly? Do other ST's even bother learning them themselves?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/231-blitzburger","name":"Blitzburger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar231_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"183"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-17T12:43:53-07:00","id":848926,"title":"","content":"I mostly tell players, &quot;such and such is the Commissioner for the Prince, so you know he's responsible for coordinating the resources of the Invictus&quot; if you give them the titles with an explanation the players will remember what the title is. Now that's if it actually matters. I think if you're playing an Invictus heavy game where this sort of thing is the defining city hierarchy then go for it, if its just for flavor have the NPC drop their title and the pcs will be wondering why anyone should care (just like most of the other covenants will), if its irrelevant you could even just say they're someone 'important' in the Invictus. <br /> <br /> I find the less book keeping on NPCs the players have to do the more likely they are going to remember who is who.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1783-spanishinquisition","name":"SpanishInquisition","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1783_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"60"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-17T12:55:25-07:00","id":848932,"title":"","content":"I love the Invictus title system and make full use of it (ie, Invictus N/PCs address one another by their titles all the time). As my game is text-based and plays out dialogue between characters line-by-line, I think we'd lose more than most games if we left it out.<br /> <br /> Not all of my players know how the title system works, which is fine. Not all of them are members of the Invictus. When they talk to Invictus NPCs, I give them Politics rolls to see if they're aware of the proper title to use. If they fail, it's not a huge breach of etiquette, as the First Estate doesn't expect outsiders to be familiar with the terms of address they use (and isn't the ruling covenant in my game's city, so they aren't in a position make everyone). I did expect the player of my former Invictus PC to be familiar with the title system, which she was, and greatly enjoyed using it and seeing it come up.<br /> <br /> I write out the full titles list for Invictus NPCs in my notes, as there's no way I'd remember them all in my head. Here's an example of the format I use:<br /> <br /> <i>Introductory:</i> \u201cThe Good Madam Adelais Seyres, Viscountess of Magazine Street, Councilor of the Inner Circle, Librettist, Notary, Speaker, Harpy, and Journeywoman of the Guild of Nemesis.\u201d<br /> <i>Formal:</i> \u201cMadam Councilor.\u201d<br /> <i>Familiar:</i> \u201cMadam Adelais.\u201d<br /> <i>Intimate:</i> \u201cAdelais.\u201d","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://blood-and-bourbon.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Blood and Bourbon</a>, my New Orleans-based Vampire chronicle.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3110-false-epiphany","name":"False Epiphany","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3110_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"748"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-17T12:59:06-07:00","id":848936,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SpanishInquisition</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/848879-question-about-storytelling-the-invictus?p=848926#post848926\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mostly tell players, &quot;such and such is the Commissioner for the Prince, so you know he's responsible for coordinating the resources of the Invictus&quot; if you give them the titles with an explanation the players will remember what the title is. Now that's if it actually matters. I think if you're playing an Invictus heavy game where this sort of thing is the defining city hierarchy then go for it, if its just for flavor have the NPC drop their title and the pcs will be wondering why anyone should care (just like most of the other covenants will), if its irrelevant you could even just say they're someone 'important' in the Invictus.<br /> <br /> I find the less book keeping on NPCs the players have to do the more likely they are going to remember who is who.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> It's rather easy, really. Most of the time, you'll get away with just knowing Master,Mister, Alder and Lord/Lady. I do use them,because that brings more roleplay into it, and it allows one to really know who's using these and who's not.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-17T15:27:57-07:00","id":849010,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blitzburger</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/848879-question-about-storytelling-the-invictus#post848879\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm curious how other ST's handle the Invictus in their campaigns, specifically if and how they play up the titles aspect, and if so, how? Do you guys just hand wave that covenant members know and are implied to be using everyone's titles, or do you actually expect players that chose to join to study and use them co\u0155rectly? Do other ST's even bother learning them themselves?</div> </div> </div> </div>I play up the title aspect. Usually when I'm introducing an Invictus NPC to the group, there will be some context to the person's titles in the scene, or worst case some kind of status/politics check to give them what the proper or minimally polite use would be. I tend not to do gotcha moments if the player messes up, and just ask them directly if they meant to not use it or just slipped up OOC. I'm more interested in making sure the ramp-up of conflict occurs via player choice rather than mistake. That being said, the more experienced the player is - especially if they have played Invictus before - the more likely I am to encourage them to really learn and understand the system.<br /> <br /> Obviously each NPC is slightly different and there are of course outliers, but in aggregate my Invictus use titles for themselves and for the other Covenants when in official or public settings. The in-character conceit is that titles are the language of Elysium. The beast doesn't use titles or etiquette rituals, so when you use them, you're showing your conversation partner that the man is fully in control. As such even though the Invictus were thrown out of ruling power 10 year ago, the title and courtesy system they use has infused the new city officers, including Carthians (to the consternation of their more fiery members).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4047-holy","name":"Holy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4047_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"274"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-18T05:18:15-07:00","id":849201,"title":"","content":"I use custom titles for my game - I fail to see why titles should remain constant from city to city. And, yeah, I use them in play. I'm not no super strict on requiring people to adhere to outdated forms of address, especially in public. Or that stupid &quot;using the word MY is a super huge insult!!&quot; thing; no one uses the word to mean possession like that in modern language, and I find it to be silly to insist that vampires who never were raised in a pseudo-Victorian culture to know or care about it. I do insist on respect around the Invictus, and using more formal / polite language. Exactly what the formal/polite language is depends on the context and the individual Invictus, but the respect thing is big. Showing proper forms of respect is everything. If an insult is done out of ignorance, that's one thing, and usually either ignored or corrected, then forgiven. If its calculated and deliberate? Rough language from a street rat is tolerated more than a subtle insult from someone polished. Intent is more important. <br /> <br /> Anyways, titles. Titles in my cities tend to run the gammut from Boss to more formal Lord to Mistress to Chief Officer. Military rank or law enforcement rank often serves for the Invictus knighthood. The Invictus, especially in 2e, are the keepers of the Masquerade. They're not going to use forms that are going to raise eyebrows.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-18T09:11:40-07:00","id":849304,"title":"","content":"So, warning: my games are apparently pretty atypical. <br /> <br /> To me, the Invictus is less about the titles than the power structures. The Invictus are almost synonymous to me with Feudalism. If the Invictus are in power, there will be a feudal system. Even if they <i>were</i> in power, that feudal structure is probably still around. Because of the structure, there are positions that call for names, and the particular city/invictus flavor will decide if those things are Duke/Countess/Baron/etc. or something more like Executive/Vice President/CFO/etc., or even something more exotic. But just because the titles exist doesn't mean people care or use them. That's also going to be a personal preference. I, so far, have never run a game where fancy titles were used and harped upon. An individual might require uppity PCs to call them by their proper address just to get in their craw and show them their place, but mostly, it's much more casual. The modern world doesn't really about titles like this, so, modern vampires mostly won't, either.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2698-the-storyteller","name":"The Storyteller","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"132"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}